summary:
- topic: Summer Learning Programs
  text: The district successfully ran diverse summer programs for students, including
    ESL, extended school year, elementary academy with Boston Museum of Science, MOLI
    initiative, high school credit recovery, and the Maine Construction Academy. These
    programs served hundreds of students, with notable achievements like 33 academic
    credits recovered and national certifications earned in construction.
- topic: Staff Professional Development
  text: Over a hundred staff members participated in extensive professional learning
    opportunities throughout the summer. Topics included math strategies, reading
    instruction, social studies, and the implementation of Positive Behavioral Interventions
    and Supports (PBIS) and Multi-Tiered System of Supports (MTSS).
- topic: School Year Preparations & District Vision
  text: Preparations for the 2024-2025 school year are underway, with bus information
    available early via the Ride 360 app. The superintendent introduced the new district
    theme, 'Together We Grow,' emphasizing collective development and a growth-focused
    approach for all members of the school community.
- topic: School Safety and Security Updates
  text: The Director of Operations and Safety provided an update on recent accomplishments
    and ongoing work in school security. This includes implementing new standard response
    procedures, conducting security audits, enhancing physical security measures,
    and customizing reunification plans for each school.
- topic: Freedom of Access Act Review
  text: Assistant Superintendent JohannaPrince led an annual review of the Freedomof
    AccessAct (Policy KDB) for board members. Individual follow-up calls will be scheduled
    to ensure all members understand the legal requirements for public proceedings
    and communications.
- topic: Financial Report and Donations
  text: The FinanceCommittee reported on July expenditures, noting that higher figures
    were due to encumbrances for the full year, reflecting a shift towards an accrual
    accounting method. The board also approved significant donations from GerryMyatt
    of EagleAssociates, SouthPortland/CapeElizabethCommunityChamber, and PapeSubaru,
    with specific uses for most funds.
- topic: Personnel Elections and Policy Approvals
  text: The board approved several key personnel elections, including a new Director
    of Mental and Behavioral Health, Special Education Teacher, School Psychologist,
    Math Specialist, Assistant Director of Instructional Support, and Behavior Strategist.
    Additionally, eighteen policies covering various aspects from learning results
    to public conduct on school property were approved on their second reading.
